<title>MEXICO: Mexico's September trade surplus $683 mln.</title>
<headline>Mexico's September trade surplus $683 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Finance Ministry said on Friday that the final September trade surplus was $683 million.  </p>
<p>The ministry released the following trade data for the month of September:</p>
<p>All figures are in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>			   Sept 96  PCT DIFF   JAN-SEPT 96  YR AGO/</p>
<p>									PCT DIFF</p>
<p>TRADE SURPLUS	  683	n/a	 5,564	 n/a</p>
<p> EXPORTS		 8,377   +20.7 pct  69,741	+19.2 pct</p>
<p>   Petroleum -	 1,098   +51.4 pct  8,294	 +28.0 pct</p>
<p>   Crude oil -	 n/a     +14.8 pct  n/a	   n/a</p>
<p>   Non-oil   -	 n/a	n/a	 n/a	   n/a</p>
<p>	Manufactures - 7,087   +17.9 pct  58,272	+20.6 pct</p>
<p>	Non-maquila  - n/a     +15.6 pct  n/a	   +23.6 pct</p>
<p>	Agriculture  - 158     -2.8 pct   2,843	 -13.7 pct</p>
<p>   Non-oil mining  - 34	 n/a	 332	   n/a</p>
<p> IMPORTS		 7,694   +26.6 pct  64,177	+20.9 pct</p>
<p>Intermediate</p>
<p>	    goods -    6,233   +24.4 pct  52,020	+21.8 pct</p>
<p>	Non maquila  - n/a	n/a	 n/a	   +21.3 pct</p>
<p>	Maquila -	n/a	n/a	 n/a	   +22.0 pct</p>
<p>   Capital goods   - 887     +37.3 pct  7,622	 +17.4 pct</p>
<p>   Consumer goods  - 574     +36.7 pct  4,535	 +16.8 pct</p>
<p>-- Mexico City Newsroom 525 7287903</p>
</text>
